  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "level": 8,
  "order": 803,
  "theme": "health",
  "culturalNote": "For anything beyond the chemist, Kenyans head to a hospital or clinic: you register at reception, see a nurse for \"vitals\", then the doctor. Doctors ask about habits (\"huwa unakunywa maji ya kutosha?\" — do you usually drink enough water?) and give if/when instructions with -ki-: \"ukiona homa inapanda, rudi\" (if you see the fever rising, come back). Relatives describe what happened: \"dawa ambayo nilipewa\" (the medicine that I was given).",
  "startingPoint": "Your stomach has been bad for three days. You're at a clinic in Kilimani, sitting with Dr Achieng.",
